
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Allowed types:
#   feat     New feature or encoding support
#   fix      Bug fix
#   perf     Performance improvement
#   refactor Code change without feature or bug fix
#   docs     Documentation changes (README, ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, doc comments)
#   test     Adding or updating specs
#   build    Build system, shard.yml, or generator tools
#   ci       CI/CD workflows or git hooks
#   chore    Maintenance tasks and config updates
#   style    Formatting / whitespace changes
#
# Optional scopes: bom, utf, single_byte, detector, tables, spec, bench, ci
#
# Rules:
#   - Use imperative mood in the subject ("add ...", not "added ...")
#   - Keep the header at or under 72 characters
#   - Do not end the subject with a period
#   - Add `!` after type/scope (or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer) for breaking changes
#
# Examples:
#   feat(utf): add BOM-less UTF-32 detection
#   fix(detector): fall back to UTF-8 when NUL input is not UTF-16
#   perf(single_byte): avoid heap allocation in prober loop
